then this is meta-case 4 mentioned earlier.
However, from the initial paper by John Clifford I can't understand what is
meant:
"Lojban has the advantage of monoparsing: that there is only one
grammatical reading of any sentence, a clear advantage."

How can {lo se xi vei pa a re no'a} be monoparsed in pragmatic terms? It
still has two readings.

{mi prami do} still has zillions of readings including {mi ba'o prami do}
and {mi ba zu ze'i ru'i prami do}.


